{
 "about": "A three-ink risograph zine: fluorescent pink, medium blue and yellow on cream stock. Every ink layer is \"blend\": \"multiply\", so overlaps mix the way inks do on paper. Misregistered plates are duplicate type offset 4–8 px with a slow \"boil\". The blob and the date are halftoned in their own ink. \"inkTexture\" gives the uneven stencil coverage and \"step\": \"threes\" gives a hand-pulled cadence. Swap the inks for real riso colours (see docs/video/craft/graphic-design.md §3) but keep it to 2–3 of them. It tends to fail when the inks are many or the type is thin. The full piece adds a reaction-diffusion shader page and uses Bricolage Grotesque.",
